{
  "rules": [
    "Apply a strong downward correction of approximately -15% to -20% when the model forecasts a steady uptrend while recent history shows high volatility and negative sentiment spikes (-0.33) preceding the forecast.",
    "Detect 'overshoot bias' where models predict linear growth after a price spike; correct by applying a mean-reversion factor that targets the lower end of the historical range rather than the trend line.",
    "Reduce forecasted returns by 40-50% when sentiment history contains negative values (-0.33) immediately before the forecast horizon, indicating market fear overrides technical trends.",
    "Avoid extrapolating recent price spikes into future horizons; instead, anchor forecasts to the moving average of the last 18 days if volatility is high and sentiment is neutral or negative.",
    "Correct upward bias by shifting the entire forecast curve downward when the true outcome shows a crash pattern (e.g., dropping below 70) despite model predictions staying above 75."
  ]
}
